    "result_text": "Done. The full build passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`, all tests green).\n\n## Summary\n\nThe acceptance test creates an owner and expects `GET /api/owners/{id}` to return `$.selfLink` = `/api/owners/{id}`. Since the owner DTOs are generated from `openapi.yml` and populated via a MapStruct mapper, I made three small, single-responsibility changes:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `selfLink` read-only string property to the `Owner` schema (so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field, consistent with the other derived fields like `displayName`, `salutation`).\n\n2. **`util/OwnerSelfLink.java`** (new) \u2014 a tiny formatter that composes `/api/owners/<id>` from the owner id (null-safe), matching the existing pattern of small formatter utils (`SalutationFormatter`, etc.).\n\n3. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added one `@Mapping` for `selfLink` delegating to `OwnerSelfLink.of(owner.getId())`, alongside the other expression-based mappings.\n\nNo controller changes were needed \u2014 every owner returned through `toOwnerDto` (get, list, create) now carries its self-link.",
